UID:d774b149e048e3ffbfa3719aff6485544fe48b19@pushpin.city
DTSTAMP:20261024T221536Z
DTSTART:20261025T200000Z
DTEND:20261025T220000Z
SUMMARY:Special Guest Gallery Chat with Traditional Medicine Practitioner B
 atul True Heart
LOCATION:Oakland Museum\, 1000 Oak St\, Oakland\, CA 94607
DESCRIPTION:Special Guest Gallery Chat with Traditional Medicine Practition
 er Batul True Heart As part of this year’s Día de los Muertos Community
  Celebration\, come sit with Batul True Heart (they/them) in OMCA’s Gall
 ery of Natural Science as they share their personal experience of practici
 ng traditional medicine in times of mourning. In this 30-minute talk\, Bat
 ul will speak about what has brought them to the path of earth-based ances
 tral medicine\, and what has been most supportive for them during times of
  deep emotional pain. You will learn about feelings from an Indigenous per
 spective and gain practical ways to connect with emotions\, the earth\, an
 d all the elements. Honoring the traditions and practices of Día de los M
 uertos\, Batul will also introduce their favorite flower\, cempoalxóchitl
 \, and how to work with it when grieving.\nhttps://museumca.org/event/spec
 ial-guest-gallery-chat-with-traditional-medicine-practitioner-batul-true-h
 eart/\nFrom Pushpin Bay Area: https://pushpin.city/bayarea/
URL:https://museumca.org/event/special-guest-gallery-chat-with-traditional-
 medicine-practitioner-batul-true-heart/
END:VEVENT
